"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-19T19:51:38Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T20:07:18Z","body":"I don't think this is the correct approach to fix the issue. Drawing functions accept floats, and text has subpixel positioning. It doesn't always have to align to the pixel grid, especially since it is useful for zooming and scaling. \nAlso most controls don't round it to an integer and they handle it fine.\n\nSee this example with a Label, Button, TextEdit, and LineEdit (I modified the StyleBox inspector to allow floats https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114217):\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4dcf230-83de-4d22-b331-2788f6ed4cb5\n\nInstead we should just use floats for the margins in TextEdit (and LineEdit).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3676333853/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]